906,"baseline":0.016753926701570682},"6":{"attempts":935,"killRate":0.08877005347593583,"baseline":0.08449197860962566},"7":{"attempts":789,"killRate":0.8871989860583016,"baseline":0.8757921419518377}}},"pileOnWeakRival":{"attempts":6905,"killRate":0.9080376538740044,"baselineKillRate":0.8928312816799421,"byChapter":{"1":{"attempts":1000,"killRate":0.847,"baseline":0.847},"2":{"attempts":1000,"killRate":0.871,"baseline":0.871},"3":{"attempts":998,"killRate":0.8787575150300602,"baseline":0.8537074148296593},"4":{"attempts":995,"killRate":0.8964824120603015,"baseline":0.8673366834170855},"5":{"attempts":985,"killRate":0.9939086294416244,"baseline":0.9644670050761421},"6":{"attempts":953,"killRate":0.9821615949632738,"baseline":0.9643231899265478},"7":{"attempts":974,"killRate":0.891170431211499,"baseline":0.8860369609856262}}},"caps":{"readerCapShare":0.04612317752060743,"unverifiedCapShare":0.003562292845483626,"armorWhaleCutShare":0.8826610433344705,"meanArmor":0.1069601137167834,"sybilWeightAvoided":9.79201982804707,"baseFloorShare":0.009915873015873005,"meanParticipation":1.2601407577947108},"assumptions":["House faces are the eight cast ids, mapped as in brief-v4-fit: Pit/Grenna, Scriptorium/Silas, Gilt/Marrow, Tidewrack/Pip, Candle/Wick, Standard/Vey, Torn Margin/Thorn, Fold/Ash & Ember.","Stake base is frozen at chapter open: clamp(100 + 25·ln(TWL / median TWL), 100 − 30, 100 + 30). This run uses clamp ±30. The ln slope stays 25. Tallies do not recompute base.","The std people-share rule is dropped. Health = base + net. Net is accumulated move weight for the chapter.","Every living House has the same daily budget B = 30. Cast weight = B × participation × duel multiplier × the Twist 6/7 budget factor. Participation = capped raw weight / full-attendance weight at 3 moves. Shop, Fortune, and Twist 11's fourth move change that rate. Headcount does not.","The Duel adds at most +10% to the multiplier. Quality is bonus points earned yesterday divided by 2 per duelist, capped at 1. A kill still adds nothing beyond the damage bars.","Twists 6 and 7 scale the budget by the old people-share odds ratio: (w′/(1−w′)) / (w/(1−w)), with w′ = w ± 0.10.","Anti-pile-on: incoming hit weight above the cap counts at half. The amount under the cap counts in full. The cap is 2× the living-House mean in chapters 1–5 and 1.5× in chapters 6–7. Twist hit multipliers apply first. Armor and the Crown apply to the softened weight. Twist 10 softens each half on its own.","Revival is once per season, total (§10.7). A later pour can still fill a bar for A1. From ch5 there is no revival, and the death penalty is charged immediately. Ch6 and ch7 eliminations are the podium and pay nothing.","Oath ×1.5 multiplies the pot stake share only. It does not multiply TWL or Health.","Unverified weight is §9, which replaces §3: min(1, stake / m), one weight per cluster. m is the median verified stake in living Houses, frozen at chapter open.","Unverified clusters are collapsed at generation: one weight from the combined stake, not one weight per sybil.","Population is the same invention as the v4 run. House size is lognormal (σ 0.50). A typical house has about 42 verified stakers (median stake 100, σ 0.65), 28 unverified (median stake 35, σ 0.85, 18% of them a 3–8 wallet cluster), and 36 free Readers.","35% of verified stakers take the Oath. 35% play the Duel at lookahead skill, 65% greedy, and 80% of stakers attempt it. The Duel multiplier is earned the day it is played and applied the next morning, including across the chapter boundary, at that chapter's thresholds.","Shop extras: 22% of stakers buy one, 6% buy two. Weight equals a normal move. Readers do not shop.","Fortune is one draw a morning, equal thirds: +1 move, Spyglass, or Doodle/fragment. The +1 weighs the same as that wallet's move. Spyglass retargets 10% of hit weight onto the current lowest rival (invented). Twist 9 sets that to 0. Doodles and fragments add 0.","Heal split, invented and unchanged: verified 62% of layer weight heals, unverified 48%, Readers 82%, ±8 points. The rest hits. Ghosts only hit.","Default hit split, invented and unchanged: 55% on the lowest-Health rival, 25% on the Crown if that is someone else, 20% across the other rivals. Day 1 of chapter 1 has no Crown. Later mornings inherit the previous Tally, including the previous chapter's snapshot.","Armor fresh locks, invented and unchanged: 10% of verified and 5% of unverified lock new Bard equal to 8–30% of their stake. A separate 15% rollover is generated and ignored. Re-pledges and switch-ins are not fresh locks.","Armor formula is min(0.60, coefficient × fresh / locked) + ward. The coefficient is 6, or 12 under Twist 3. One wallet supplies at most 20% of that pre-cap formula armor. Ward is at most 0.10. The total cap stays 0.70.","Ward, invented and unchanged: 45% of houses buy a Ward each day, uniform from 0 to 0.10.","Raise, invented and unchanged: about 18% of verified wallets Raise each chapter, at 15% of stake. If the house is shortlisted, 45% of those raisers go to 4× and the rest stay at 2×, and only if the house survives that chapter.","raise_loyalty_pays stays false (§10.8). Pot Loyalty is then raw heal weight. The true-flag comparison still stacks day-3 shortlist heals at 1.5× and a surviving raiser at 2× or 4×. Health does not use either flag.","Inside a finishing House the pot is 70% stake-time (Oath ×1.5) and 30% Loyalty, verified humans only, then capped at 2% per wallet with the surplus shared by the uncapped wallets.","Re-pledge, invented and unchanged: 18% of a dead House's verified and 10% of its unverified move to a random living House at the next chapter open, after the penalty, with time restarted and the Oath cleared. 25% of its Readers follow. This is not Armor.","Ghost retention, invented and unchanged: 72% of verified wallets who did not re-pledge keep hitting, verified only. Their hit weight is B × (ghosts / verified at death) × 0.5 × (1 + 1/3), so a large dead House does not out-hit a small one. A6's denominator is that House's verified wallets at the snapshot, before re-pledge, and the bar is 60%.","TWL uses chapter-open locks at weight 1. Fresh locks weigh the fraction of the chapter still ahead (day 1: 5/6, day 2: 1/2, day 3: 1/6). Move weight uses chapter-open stake, frozen with m.","Even-count medians are the mean of the two central values. A Health tie breaks to the lower TWL, then the lower cast id.","The Twist deck deals 7 distinct Twists per season. The forced-Twist study turns one Twist on for every chapter.","Twist 8 draws the snapshot uniformly from +56h to +66h. The day-3 Tally is +59h (chapter start 10:00, day 3 starts +48h, tally 21:00). Day-3 moves count only when the drawn hour is at least 59.","Twist 11 gives stakers a 4th move. Readers stay at one move.","Twist 12 uses Duel bars of 40% and 55% instead of 50% and 65%.","Duel boss HP is fitted per chapter in duel-sim.mjs. D1 and D2 use that HP. D3 stays on the engine's 0.9 scale, and D2 still starts with 10 guard.","Large House, for the pile-on, is unchanged: most verified wallets. The rich rival is the highest-TWL other House. The poor rival is the lowest-TWL other House. The target is retargeted each chapter from that morning's living set. A kill counts only when the target is alive in the paired no-pile season and stays dead.","Top 3 is the set of Houses alive at the start of chapter 6 when that set has three Houses. The lowest-stake House is the chapter-1 minimum TWL.","Duel bonus rates are the per-chapter shared-seed rates in results/duel.json. +1 is 50% damage and +2 is 65% (Twist 12: 40% and 55%). A kill adds nothing extra."],"ambiguities":["The attached s0-house-delta ends at §10.8. It does not contain §11 or §11.6. The v3 bullets in the task are applied. The earlier open readings stay locked as the rules below, rather than being re-guessed.","Anti-pile-on halves only the excess above the cap. Chapters 1–5 use 2× the mean. Chapters 6–7 use 1.5×.","A5 stays the chapter sum of effective hits and heals on each morning's Crown. The annotation line says \"one turn.\"","Twist 8 is still drawn from +56h to +66h. The day-3 Tally is +59h, so day-3 moves count only when the drawn hour is at least 59. §10.7 also says the window always opens after that Tally.","The Duel HP fit is unchanged. D3 stays on the engine's 0.9 scale. D2 still starts with 10 guard.","m is the stake balance. Full-day locks use that balance as the 24h weight.","Unverified stakes pay the 40% death penalty. Oath 25% is verified only.","The 2% pot surplus is shared by the uncapped verified wallets.","A Reader's Fortune +1 weighs 0.5 and sits inside the Reader cap.","Twist 10 retargets the afternoon half after the midday Tally. Each half is softened alone.","Twist 11 gives stakers a fourth move, which raises participation against a 3-move denominator. Readers stay at one move.","The first morning has no Crown."]}